        171.6273956298828
      ],
      "text": "Daily isoniazid monotherapy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        171.3824005126953,
        527.4168701171875,
        185.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "The efficacy of six months daily isoniazid monotherapy (6H) in different populations and settings",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        185.3824005126953,
        527.4227294921875,
        199.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "has been shown in a number of systematic reviews  . A systematic review of RCTs in  (49, 69, 70)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.3824005126953,
        527.41796875,
        213.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "people living with HIV showed isoniazid monotherapy reduces the overall risk for TB by 33% (RR",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        213.3824005126953,
        527.4199829101562,
        227.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "0.67; 95% CI: 0.51–0.87), and that the preventive efficacy reached 64% for people with a positive",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.3824005126953,
        527.42236328125,
        241.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "TST (RR 0.36; 95% CI: 0.22–0.61)  . Furthermore, the efficacy of the 6-month regimen was not  (49)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        241.3824005126953,
        524.3994140625,
        255.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "significantly different from that of 12 months’ daily isoniazid monotherapy (RR 0.58; 95% CI: 0.3–",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        255.3824005126953,
        527.4178466796875,
        269.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "1.12). A systematic review of RCTs also showed a significantly greater reduction in TB incidence",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        269.38238525390625,
        527.4190063476562,
        283.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "among participants given the 6-month regimen than in those given a placebo (odds ratio (OR) 0.65;",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        283.38238525390625,
        527.4019775390625,
        297.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "95% CI: 0.50–0.83)  . No controlled clinical trials were found of daily isoniazid monotherapy for 9  (71)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        297.38238525390625,
        527.3883056640625,
        311.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "months (9H) versus 6H. Re-analysis and modelling of the United States Public Health Service trials of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        311.38238525390625,
        527.4188842773438,
        325.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "isoniazid conducted in the 1950s and 1960s, however, showed that the benefit of isoniazid increases",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        325.3824157714844,
        527.4253540039062,
        339.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "progressively when it is given for up to 9–10 months and stabilizes thereafter  . For this reason,  (72)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.3824157714844,
        443.2535705566406,
        353.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "9H is retained as an alternative regimen to 6H in the recommended TPT options.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        367.2724304199219,
        321.40203857421875,
        381.6274108886719
      ],
      "text": "Daily rifampicin plus isoniazid for 3 months (3HR)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        381.3824157714844,
        527.4221801757812,
        395.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "A systematic review updated in 2017 showed that the efficacy and the safety profile of 3–4 months’",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        395.3824157714844,
        527.42822265625,
        409.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "daily rifampicin plus isoniazid were similar to those of 6 months’ isoniazid  . A previous GDG  (71, 73)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        409.3824157714844,
        527.4178466796875,
        423.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "therefore strongly recommended that daily rifampicin plus isoniazid could be used as an alternative",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        423.3824157714844,
        430.0946044921875,
        437.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "to isoniazid in settings with a TB incidence < 100 per 100 000 population  .  (74)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        451.2724304199219,
        313.361083984375,
        465.6274108886719
      ],
      "text": "Daily rifampicin monotherapy for 4 months (4R)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        465.3824157714844,
        527.4213256835938,
        479.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "A previous systematic review conducted for the 2015 guidelines on TPT and updated in 2017,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        479.3824157714844,
        527.4215698242188,
        493.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "found similar efficacy for 3–4 months’ daily rifampicin and 6H (OR 0.78; 95% CI: 0.41–1.46)  .  (71, 73)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        493.3824157714844,
        527.4114379882812,
        507.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "The review also showed that individuals given rifampicin daily for 3–4 months had a lower risk for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        507.3824462890625,
        491.1882629394531,
        521.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "hepatotoxicity than those treated with isoniazid monotherapy (OR 0.03; 95% CI: 0.00–0.48).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        535.3824462890625,
        527.3873291015625,
        549.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "In 2019, the GDG discussed the implications of using 4R in high TB burden settings based on",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        549.3824462890625,
        527.4188842773438,
        563.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "findings from RCTs of 4R vs 9H that included adults and children from such countries  . In study  (75-78)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        563.3824462890625,
        527.416748046875,
        577.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "participants > 17 years, the difference in rate of confirmed TB between 4R and 9H (4R arm minus",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        577.3823852539062,
        527.4212646484375,
        591.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "9H arm) was < 0.01 cases per 100 person-years (95% CI: −0.14 to –0.16); the difference in treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        591.3823852539062,
        527.4199829101562,
        605.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "completion was 15.1% (95% CI: 12.7–17.4); the difference for Grade 3–5 adverse events was −1.1%",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        605.3823852539062,
        527.419921875,
        619.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "(95% CI: −1.9 to –0.4). In individuals < 18 years, the difference in rate of TB disease between 4R",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        619.3823852539062,
        527.4234008789062,
        633.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "and 9H was –0.37 cases per 100 person-years (95% CI: −0.88 to 0.14); the difference in treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        633.3823852539062,
        527.4476318359375,
        647.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "completion was 13.4% (95% CI: 7.5–19.3); the difference in risk for adverse events attributed to the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        647.3823852539062,
        430.55731201171875,
        661.8253784179688
      ],
      "text": "medicine used and resulting in discontinuation was −0.0 (95% CI: −0.1 to 0.1).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
